    <values>
        <!-- Bare "GLBM" REMOVED 22 Jul: it is the bundle CONTAINER, never the invoiced line. Verified
             across 18 quotes Apr-Jul the container promo/dispatch are ALWAYS blank and the CHILD
             ("GLBM - Team Membership" / "- Individual Membership") carries MSHP. Because the container
             is not a child it passed the child-exclusion test, so the engine stamped MSHP/ME onto it
             (Q-217531, 19 Jul) - inverting the convention. The two membership codes stay in scope; they
             are children so the engine still skips them and reps hand-type MSHP exactly as before.
             Automating the child (a Derive_Child_Product_Codes setting, like the Mid Market Pro carve-out)
             is a deliberate enhancement, not a regression fix - do that separately. -->
        <field>ALM_Product_Codes__c</field>
        <value xsi:type="xsd:string">LAWM;LWKM;GLBM - Team Membership;GLBM - Individual Membership;NYLM;NYOM;Law.com Pro;PCEM;LNVM;LGCM;LGLM;LRCM;VSCM;WEB;TIOM;DROM;RCOM;TALM;ALLM;CHLM;DBOM;NJOM;NJLM</value>
    </values>
    <values>
        <field>Segment_Promo_Product_Codes__c</field>
        <value xsi:type="xsd:string">LAWM;LWKM;Law.com Pro;NYLM;NYOM;LNVM;LGCM;LGLM;LRCM;VSCM;WEB;TIOM;DROM;RCOM;TALM;ALLM;CHLM;DBOM;NJOM;NJLM</value>
    </values>
    <values>
        <!-- ONLY products whose dispatch the engine can AUTO-FILL belong here (GLBM family -> ME,
             NYLM -> PO). Those can never leave a gap, so the backstop can never block on them.

             INVARIANT: every code listed here MUST have an active ALM_Code_Map Dispatch row. Then the
             engine always fills it, no line can ever gap, and the save-time Custom Error can never fire.

             DO NOT RE-ADD LAWM / LWKM. Their dispatch is genuinely non-deterministic (LAWM: ON 33% / OE 32%
             / OS 17% / OL 11% over 6,807 lines; LWKM similar), which is why their Dispatch rows are
             Active=false. With no way to fill them, the "backstop" is not a backstop - it fires on EVERY
             blank line. Live on 22 Jul that produced reps with quotes that would not save, and - because
             the Custom Error is raised after-save in a flow - an unhandled SBQQ.ValidationException through
             CPQ ServiceRouter that emailed 4 admins per occurrence (Saurabh Patil 14:43; Andrew Barsody).
             Pre-REV-60 a blank Law.com dispatch was allowed for everyone bar 2-3 named reps, so mandating
             it org-wide was never the ask. If the business does want it mandatory, implement it as a scoped
             CPQ Validation Product Rule (native QLE message, fires BEFORE save) - NOT via this field.

             NYOM stays listed because it now auto-fills: 4,806 historical lines are 74.7% ON and 90.0%
             ON-family, so ON is a safe write-on-blank default (a rep's OS/OE is never overwritten). -->
        <field>Dispatch_Required_Product_Codes__c</field>
        <value xsi:type="xsd:string">GLBM - Team Membership;GLBM - Individual Membership;NYLM;NYOM</value>
    </values>
    <values>
        <!-- Grandfathering cutoff for the re-armed LAWM/LWKM/NYOM dispatch backstop, set at the
             Mon 20 Jul staffed hardening window (go-live was Fri 17 Jul; the backstop ran softened
             over the weekend). Lines created BEFORE this instant are never hard-blocked; only
             genuinely new lines must carry a dispatch. It is deliberately the RE-ARM instant, not
             go-live: the ~914 legacy open quotes AND everything quoted during the softened weekend
             window are grandfathered. Blank would mean "enforce on every line" and would
             retroactively block all of them - never clear this without re-checking. -->
        <field>Enforce_Dispatch_After__c</field>
        <value xsi:type="xsd:dateTime">2026-07-20T15:35:00.000Z</value>
    </values>
    <values>
        <field>Dispatch_Backstop_Hint__c</field>
